  <content>
  <section><para>For questions 1 – 6, use the given graph and scenario:</para>
<blockquote>
  <para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/035b6f8b53155d20a84c2a6e62831f0db3bac6bb"/></media></figure></para>
  <para>A club is selling snacks at a track meet. Oranges cost $1 each and protein bars cost $4 each. They sell a total of 100 items, and collect $304.</para>
</blockquote>

<!--Q#1-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What do you notice? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
    <list>
      <item> There are two lines. </item>
      <item> It’s about snacks. </item>
      <item> The lines intersect. </item>
      <item> The point of intersection is labeled \((32, 68)\). </item>
      <item> The sum of 32 and 68 is 100. </item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#2-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What do you wonder?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
    <para>Things students may wonder:</para>
    <list>
      <item> What does each line mean? </item>
      <item> What does the point of intersection mean? </item>
      <item> Where can you see the information from the problem on the graph? </item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<section class="check-understanding"><title>Warm Up Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="0e4967e0-47aa-4365-a3a3-273c127972be"><problem><para>
      <para>What is the approximate \(y\)–intercept of the green dashed line?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>76</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 76</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
